{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old","id":1502181,"title":"Is the V5 rulebook an appropriate gift for a 19 year old?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-05T00:24:10-08:00","id":1502181,"title":"Is the V5 rulebook an appropriate gift for a 19 year old?","content":"Last Thursday my eldest niece made a joke about going through a vampire phase and over the next couple of days I wondered how she would react to Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I asked for her email address so I could send her the rulebook, but now I'm having second thoughts. As I mentioned in the title, my niece is nineteen, so technically she is old enough. But whether its because she's my niece, or because I'm way into middle age, part of me is suddenly doubting myself. <br /> <br /> How old would someone have to be before you felt comfortable introducing them to the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T01:26:22-08:00","id":1502184,"title":"","content":"I started with VtM way younger than that... so I'm not sure how great I am to weigh in much. Ultimately? You kind of have to know your audience here. There are kids and young adults that can handle it just fine, others that might need a few years more to appreciate it, and others still that might never really click with the material.<br /> <br /> One thing you didn't mention... is she already a TT RPG gamer? Or has she expressed interest in them before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T02:36:57-08:00","id":1502186,"title":"","content":"Should be fine,v5 corebook isn't exactly user friendly so you may want to consider how bookish she is but in terms of age appropriate you're good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 02-05-2023, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T04:08:34-08:00","id":1502189,"title":"","content":"I'd rather get v20 or 1e or 2e because they're better for that age group and in general but I don't see why it'd be a problem for a 19 year old: old enough to drink (in sane countries), Old enough to go to war, old enough to star in porn... you're dealing with what is legally known as an &quot;adult&quot; (though I'm quite convinced adulthood really begins in the 30s.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T04:23:04-08:00","id":1502191,"title":"","content":"I was 14 years old when I started playing Vampire 2nd. Edition. Great times...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T07:40:02-08:00","id":1502204,"title":"","content":"I was a freshman in high school, so 13 at the time, when I started playing VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T07:49:26-08:00","id":1502206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502184#post1502184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started with VtM way younger than that... so I'm not sure how great I am to weigh in much. Ultimately? You kind of have to know your audience here. There are kids and young adults that can handle it just fine, others that might need a few years more to appreciate it, and others still that might never really click with the material.<br /> <br /> One thing you didn't mention... is she already a TT RPG gamer? Or has she expressed interest in them before?</div> </div> </div> </div>She is not an RPG player. She mostly watches anime and if it wasn't for her joke about a Vampire phase, I probably wouldn't have even considered it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T08:21:07-08:00","id":1502207,"title":"","content":"Absolutely not. Get her V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T08:36:10-08:00","id":1502208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502206#post1502206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She is not an RPG player. She mostly watches anime and if it wasn't for her joke about a Vampire phase, I probably wouldn't have even considered it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd consider what your/her other relatives would say; if you're known as the constant-gamer, and have a good relationship, yeah. She might like it, then again, she might not and it will be used to balance out a table-wobble. <br /> <br /> In high-school, years ago, one of my relatives gave me the Gamma-World box-set because they got it as a gift, in the early '80's and didn't play it, or even open it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T10:36:22-08:00","id":1502219,"title":"","content":"I was younger then 19 when I got into gaming and Anne Rice and Bram Stokers Dracula vampire stories and related material. I think it shouldn\u2019t be a problem for her as a gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T10:45:27-08:00","id":1502220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502207#post1502207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely not. Get her V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I still get V20 as a physical book? Because on DrivethruRpg, V5 is only available as a pdf now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T12:13:09-08:00","id":1502224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502220#post1502220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can I still get V20 as a physical book? Because on DrivethruRpg, V5 is only available as a pdf now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are not maybe german speakers? Cause Ulisses Spiele, the german publisher for WoD is now printing another series of V20GRW","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T12:16:52-08:00","id":1502226,"title":"","content":"We are not <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26160\" data-vbnamecard=\"26160\">Koronus</a>. My niece and I are stranded in the middle of Redneck Alberta, Canada.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T12:30:22-08:00","id":1502228,"title":"","content":"I would go with V5, as something with an appropriate level of crunch, metaplot and availability for someone who is not already into RPGs.<br /> <br /> As for age, I've just ran New Blood and The Dying Fields to a group of 16yo girls, and they went just fine, so a 19yo who likes Vampires should have no particular problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T12:50:16-08:00","id":1502229,"title":"","content":"Good to see another Canadian here on the boards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T14:11:06-08:00","id":1502239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502206#post1502206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She is not an RPG player. She mostly watches anime and if it wasn't for her joke about a Vampire phase, I probably wouldn't have even considered it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think this is plenty of reason not to get her a Vampire RPG unless you want to poke around more to figure out if she might be into it.<br /> <br /> There's been a few hit anime (or anime-inspired shows not made in Japan) that are either about vampires or have prominent vampires in them lately; on top of a pretty large list of vampire anime classics. Like anime in general, vampire themed anime can range from quirky slice of life silliness to dark gritty gory horror fests.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be worried about her age in all this, but I would be worried about jumping from what sounded like a fairly off-handed comment to shelling out for a physical copy of a 430 page book that might have nothing to do with any of her actual interests. Do you know what the last three anime she watched and liked were (vampire related or not)? If not, I'd steer away from this option. Even if she'd get into RPGs you need one that actually appeals to her tastes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T14:24:31-08:00","id":1502242,"title":"","content":"Funny thing is, I can't even find a physical copy. DriveThrurpg only sells the pdf, and the only local store that I could imagine selling it closed last September. I know the local chain bookstore didn't have it, I just checked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T15:07:59-08:00","id":1502248,"title":"","content":"You can still buy a physical copy of V20.<br /> For somebody you can't be sure will be into it that does strike me as a rather overwhelming tome to gift, but it is the more comprehensive version. Up to you.<br /> <br /> As somebody who introduced a younger relative (and other family) to the setting, I understand the feeling of second guessing the decision. 19 is definitely old enough though and there's no harm giving it a shot, imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T15:13:10-08:00","id":1502250,"title":"","content":"I meant I couldn't find a physical copy of V5.<br /> <br /> Maybe I can give her a V20 book, it's just V20 still has Assamites, Giovanni, and Followers of Set, rather than their modernized versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 02-05-2023, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T15:20:32-08:00","id":1502251,"title":"","content":"Ah, typos. Well I don't know about DrivethruRPG, but you can still buy hardbacks.<br /> <br /> I also got a laugh just now when I found it on Amazon.<i> &quot;<b>Adults, Family and Kids 13 Years Old and Up</b>.&quot;</i> Yes, this is a totally family fun game for people barely into puberty(!) (I mean I was a little younger than that when I got interested in the setting, but I still wouldn't call it kid appropriate.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T16:58:05-08:00","id":1502258,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, Vampire anime can range from slice-of-life to gritty. So depending on the vampire anime she watches, for example, if it is a comedic slice-of-life, she may not enjoy the content of VTM. Some of the content within the VTM gameline can also make people feel uncomfortable, I myself have felt somewhat uncomfortable when reading through some of the supplements.<br /> <br /> My relatives actually got me a ttrpg box for a game I was interested in. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2521_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2521\" data-vbnamecard=\"2521\">Iguazu</a> however, I never played with it. \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 02-05-2023, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T17:04:48-08:00","id":1502261,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said, Vampire anime can range from slice-of-life to gritty. So depending on the vampire anime she watches, for example, if it is a comedic slice-of-life, she may not enjoy the content of VTM. Some of the content within the VTM gameline can also make people feel uncomfortable, I myself have felt somewhat uncomfortable when reading through some of the supplements.<br /> <br /> My relatives actually got me a ttrpg box for a game I was interested in. I opened it, but like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2521_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2521\" data-vbnamecard=\"2521\">Iguazu</a>, I never played with it.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T22:38:52-08:00","id":1502284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old#post1502181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Last Thursday my eldest niece made a joke about going through a vampire phase and over the next couple of days I wondered how she would react to Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> I asked for her email address so I could send her the rulebook, but now I'm having second thoughts. As I mentioned in the title, my niece is nineteen, so technically she is old enough. But whether its because she's my niece, or because I'm way into middle age, part of me is suddenly doubting myself.<br /> <br /> How old would someone have to be before you felt comfortable introducing them to the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>So I have a little bit of a different suggestion in light of the different advice everyone has given to you in this thread until now.<br /> <br /> You were saying she is not an RPG player (yet) and she likes anime. Introducing her to the themes of the WOD with a huge tome of rules and lore (does not matter which edition) might not be the right way.<br /> <br /> So may I humbly suggest to get her the Anime (or better yet the Manga if she likes to read Manga) &quot;<b>Shiki</b>&quot;. It is probably my favroite Vampire Anime / Manga. It deals expertly with the themes common to VTM like Personal Horror, Man vs. Beast, Thirst, the Masquerade and if your into VTR or V5 even Touchstones. Storywise it is a japanese Version of &quot;Salems lot&quot; if you are familiar. WOD-wise it could be seen as a very subtle Sabbat incursion into a small japanese town to create shovelheads.<br /> <br /> IMHO if she likes the mood and themes of &quot;Shiki&quot; she will probably like VTM. So maybe test the waters with something familiar, like Shiki, and if she enjoys it get her V20/V5, or whatever you deem appropriate, next birthday/christmas/holiday/time. If you are unsure wtach it for yourself first <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T22:39:49-08:00","id":1502285,"title":"","content":"IDK about you guys but most 19 year old girls I knew favoured watching trashy torture-porn horror movies on the regular, and this certainly wasn't a phenomena unique to certain groups. Outside of Black Dog titles, I don't think there's anything in Vampire that'll really phase them. While there are exceptions and I do know a couple of women who don't respond well to horror, I think it's a little comedically na\u00efve to pretend it's too much for a<i> youth of the gentler sex </i>to enjoy books that aren't anywhere near as graphic as the films they probably watch. Given that she does like vampires it's more than likely she isn't in the squeamish category. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T22:52:48-08:00","id":1502286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502285#post1502285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IDK about you guys but most 19 year old girls I knew favoured watching trashy torture-porn horror movies on the regular, and this certainly wasn't a phenomena unique to certain groups. Outside of Black Dog titles, I don't think there's anything in Vampire that'll really phase them. While there are exceptions and I do know a couple of women who don't respond well to horror, I think it's a little comedically na\u00efve to pretend it's too much for a<i> youth of the gentler sex </i>to enjoy books that aren't anywhere near as graphic as the films they probably watch. Given that she does like vampires it's more than likely she isn't in the squeamish category.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, so she might not be interested in playing a game about draping herself over a fainting couch and bemoaning her fate because she's been turned into a blood-sucking monster. V5 might not be a great fit, is what I mean.<br /> <br /> To be honest (if that singular, offhand comment is anything to go by) she sounds like she's got a mindset more similar to mine; to wit, &quot;Oh I have sweet vampire abilities now? Cool, let's go grab unlife by the horns/explore the metaphysics of this/paint the town red!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27305-joanna_crone","name":"Joanna_Crone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T23:35:59-08:00","id":1502288,"title":"","content":"Except none of us are saying that. Hellsing Ultimate could be her favorite anime, and no edition of VtM is going to do that level of over the top gore and violence justice.<br /> <br /> We're not talking about how a 19 year old woman has to be &quot;protected&quot; from the horrors of VtM. We're saying, &quot;19 year old and female that likes vampire anime&quot; tells you pretty much nothing about whether she's going to like VtM, because vampire anime is so broad in what genres it can get into.<br /> <br /> Nobody has used her gender as a reason not to get her V5, there's near universal agreement that 19 s plenty old enough to handle it, and the closest thing to puritanical I can see in the thread is just being careful about what other members of her family might think; since presumably a present might get opened in front of older family members that might not approve and thus cause drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T08:29:10-08:00","id":1502307,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25379\" data-vbnamecard=\"25379\">Spacedigger</a> gave you some solid additional advice: you may also try to run a short introductory solo game for her, perhaps adapting <i>Monsters, New Blood</i>or an old classic like <i>Alien Hunger, </i>to help her get into RPGs before proposing a thick corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T10:25:19-08:00","id":1502312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502288#post1502288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except none of us are saying that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was just knee-jerk horrified by the idea of someone being worried about giving V5 to someone as a gift, but we're not actually allowed to talk about how it's a terrible gift so I just went the other direction. IMO if someone gave me V5 i'd probably take it as some kind of passive aggressive gift. Imagine being a huge superman fan and someone gifts you Zack Snyder's<i> Batman V Superman: Dawn of Justice.</i><br /> <br /> That and being relatively young myself (with younger siblings) honestly I think V5 leans more towards a caricature of what kids these days want than what they actually want. Like watching a modern teen drama obviously written by 40 year olds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 02-06-2023, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T14:14:43-08:00","id":1502324,"title":"","content":"You are allowed to just.... not post? I know I probably don't seem like someone that exercises a lot of restraint, but I probably just skip posting something twice as often as I actually post (not including times I meant to respond to someone but spaced). <br /> <br /> We're also not talking about if V5 core is an appropriate gift for a huge fan of, say, Bloodlines 1, who might not know the TT RPG well, but already has some strong feelings about the setting and concepts; let alone someone buying V5 for either of us. For all the problems both of us have with V5 (and I doubt any regular poster around here doesn't know how strongly we feel about it), lots of people still like it. For all either of us knows, it would be the perfect gift for her despite being a massive shot in the dark. Ultimately it's not in our hands, and it doesn't really impact our lives one way or the other if the choice of gift is V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T21:03:51-08:00","id":1502339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502250#post1502250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant I couldn't find a physical copy of V5.<br /> <br /> Maybe I can give her a V20 book, it's just V20 still has Assamites, Giovanni, and Followers of Set, rather than their modernized versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't worry too much about that. The Assamites and Setities haven't really changed much in V5 (outside of mechanical changes) and even the change in allegiances isn't really the entire Clans as the groups depicted in V5 Camarilla and Anarchs are breakaway groups. And in the case of the Assamites, their defectors joining the Cam has been a thing since the Rev Ed like twenty years ago.<br /> <br /> Of the three the Giovanni have had the biggest changes but really it's just the consolidation of the Bloodlines of Death into a single Clan/Cult/Sect and the internal political changes with that. But unless you think she's going to really gravitate towards the Giovanni/Hecata, again I wouldn't worry about that. And even if she did, seeing what they were and what they are now wouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1502181-is-the-v5-rulebook-an-appropriate-gift-for-a-19-year-old?p=1502307#post1502307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25379\" data-vbnamecard=\"25379\">Spacedigger</a> gave you some solid additional advice: you may also try to run a short introductory solo game for her, perhaps adapting <i>Monsters, New Blood</i>or an old classic like <i>Alien Hunger, </i>to help her get into RPGs before proposing a thick corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I second this. If she has no interest in the game, the present will be nothing more than an overpriced paper weight. It would be better to have her experience the game first and if she likes it, get her the Rulebook.<br /> <br /> New Blood from the Starter Pack would probably be the best for V5 as it's really designed to bring new players into VtM, with their PCs getting Embraced and thrust into their new existence.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T10:57:11-08:00","id":1502400,"title":"","content":"Perhaps you should give your niece a quick rundown on the setting and the main clans and what they stand for and see what her interest is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T13:51:55-08:00","id":1502429,"title":"","content":"A core book might not be the best place to start for somebody who doesn't play TTRPGs, regardless of whether ultimately playing it is the point. Maybe you could pick one of the novels, chronicles or video games first, <i>then</i> get the core or even a supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-07T18:48:38-08:00","id":1502474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__l